# Algorithm_01: Most important point
## Goal
Find the most "important" point in a given data set.
- Read a file of data
- Weigh each point based on how many primary, secondary, etc connections it has
## Extra
- Make it a template to work with any {VARIABLE, VARIABLE[]} hashmap
- Add a relationship diagram for visual aid of the data
# Changes planned
- Switch from std::unordered_map to just the network class
- Pass std::ifstream into network constructor
- Change network.connections from std::pair to just std::vector representing all connections between points
